# .gitignore for the NVDA add-on

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
# CAUTION: NO *.py[cod] rule - the "d" would also exclude the *.pyd files,
# that is the compiled C extensions in lib/_arch/. Without them a fresh
# clone does not run (aiohttp, yarl, pycryptodomex ...).
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
# Produced by "build_addon.py relnotes" in the release workflow
release-notes.md
# Backup that "build_addon.py libs" creates before replacing lib/
lib.old/

# NVDA
*.nvda-addon
# The .pot is the template for translators and ships inside the package -
# it is checked in, not ignored.
*.mo
# CAUTION: the compiled .mo IS the file NVDA loads at runtime - the .po is
# only the source. Without this exception a fresh clone of the repository
# builds an add-on with NO translations, and build_addon.py does not notice.
# The exception has to come after the *.mo rule (the last rule wins).
!locale/**/*.mo

# Logs
*.log
log_tail.txt
NVDA_LOG.log
# A tester's log arrives under whatever name and extension the mail client
# gave it, and it carries their address and their encrypted credentials.
# `*.log` alone let an NVDA_LOG_<name>.txt through.
NVDA_LOG*

# Development
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.claude/

# Temporary files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Personal data (IMPORTANT)
config.ini
settings.json
# Runtime data of the add-on (normally in the addons folder, but during
# development occasionally here)
SmartHomeControl_history.json*
SmartHomeControl_energy.json*
SmartHomeControl_favorites.json*
smarthomecontrol_salt.bin

# Internal working documents (not for the public repository). Only README,
# CHANGELOG, LICENSE and THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES belong in the repository -
# everything else is working material.
VEROEFFENTLICHUNG.md
README_FAKTENPRUEFUNG.md
VOR_EINREICHUNG_CHECKLISTE.md
SmartHomeControl_Fehleranalyse.md
SmartHomeControl_Release_Checkliste.md
BACKLOG_NACH_RELEASE_1.md
CODE_REVIEW_*.md

# Library sources unpacked from upstream (reproduced through
# requirements-bundle.txt, not checked in)
MerossIot-*/
pyvesync/

# SCons
.sconsign.dblite
.sconf_temp/

# Working material that does not belong in the public repository: the
# project notes. They travel to the other machines over Synology Drive, not
# over git.
#
# tools/checks/ is the exception and belongs in here: those scripts are the
# add-on's memory of every fault it has had, they need neither NVDA nor an
# account, and the workflow runs them on every push. On one disk and run by
# hand they were worth much less.
CLAUDE.md
tools/*
!tools/checks/
